un así lo define como «nihilismo tecnológico». Weinstein abre el libro con este catálogo de desprecios porque coincide con el de sus enemigos del otro extremo: la crítica liberal y la derecha religiosa no se ponen de acuerdo en qué condenar, pero sí en condenarlo, y eso es lo que despierta el interés sociológico del libro.","color":"#60a5fa","family":"Detractores, censura y pánico moral","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/HeavyMetal/#critica-progresista"}],"book_tracks":[],"mentions":[],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"\"Very Natty Dressed\"","body":"Robert Palmer was noted for his sartorial style, described as \"very natty dressed.\" \"Or the very Natalie Dressed Robert Palmer who took addicted to love to number one in early 86.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"The British Are Charting Edition Part 2","url":null},{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"The British Are Charting Edition Part 2","url":"https://shows.acast.com/hit-parade/episodes/695d4f7a154465cd600c7ae7"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Ocean Center Concert (July 17)","body":"Robert Palmer performed his \"blue-eyed soul\" brand of music at the Ocean Center in Daytona Beach on Thursday, July 17, with a showtime of 8 p.m. The event was advertised to include a special guest. \"Robert Palmer brings his brand of blue I'd sold the Ocean Center in Daytona Beach Thursday July 17th Showtime for Robert Palmer is 8 p.m.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Weird History of Concert Tickets Part 2","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8q2bRZyHnHE"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"St. Petersburg Concert (August 15)","body":"Robert Palmer was also scheduled to perform in St. Petersburg on August 15, presented as a \"phantasma concert.\" \"And see Robert Palmer to be front in St. Peter's Burj and I have 15 a phantasma concert presentation.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Weird History of Concert Tickets Part 2","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8q2bRZyHnHE"}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[{"kind":"concert","title":"Ocean Center (July 17)","body":null,"year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[]},{"kind":"concert","title":"St. Petersburg (August 15)","body":null,"year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[]}],"xref":[{"kind":"xref","title":"Exemplar of 1980s Drum Sound","body":"The band, featuring Robert Palmer, members of Duran Duran, and drummer Tony Thompson, is highlighted as a prime example of the pervasive drum sound of the 1980s. This sound was characterized by its big, boomy, and powerful quality, often achieved by recording in large, reverberant rooms and augmenting with electronic effects like gated reverbs. \"The Power Station featuring Robert Palmer, a couple of guys from Durandoran and drummer Tony Thompson. That is an example of the drum sound that was very much invoked in the 1980s.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"The Power Station","from_id":271158011166249,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Music Questions People Almost Never Ask","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TsiYLGGSJ2U"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Post-Muffins Career in UK","body":"After leaving Martha and the Muffins, Martha Ladly moved to the UK, where she pursued recording, joined Robert Palmer's band, and collaborated with Elbamar designer Peter Saville, known for his work with Factory Records bands like Joy Division and New Order. \"As she quit, she moved to the UK, did some recording, joined up with Robert Palmer's band, did work with Elba Martin designer Peter Savil, the guy who did so much for factory records bands like Joy Division and New Order.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Martha Ladly","from_id":19467040054174,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Where Are They Now? Part 4","url":"https://www.youtu